    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0076" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Tripp.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge receipt of your Nos.
                    50 and 51, of the 29th ultimo and 1st instant, in relation to the claim of Mr.
                    E. W. Mix against the Austrian Government growing out of his arrest on suspicion
                    of being a Russian spy.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your conclusion that upon the facts this Government would
                    not be warranted in making a claim against the Austrian Government on behalf of
                    Mr. Mix for damages. By taking photographs at Przemysl he violated the law in
                    force there, and however innocent in his intentions or ignorant of the law he
                    may have been, his acts subjected him to the arrest and annoyance which he
                    suffered. His release was by your exertions effected as soon as could possibly
                    have been expected, and meantime no harsh or unreasonable treatment seems to
                    have been experienced by him.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
